{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 9,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Of a truth I know that it is so:But how can man be just with God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If he be pleased to contend with him,\nHe cannot answer him one of a thousand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wise in heart, and mighty in strength:\nWho hath hardened himself against him, and prospered?—",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that removeth the mountains, and they know it not,\nWhen he overturneth them in his anger;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That shaketh the earth out of its place,\nAnd the pillars thereof tremble;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That commandeth the sun, and it riseth not,\nAnd sealeth up the stars;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That alone stretcheth out the heavens,\nAnd treadeth upon the waves of the sea;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That maketh the Bear, Orion, and the Pleiades,\nAnd the chambers of the south;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That doeth great things past finding out,\nYea, marvellous things without number.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, he goeth by me, and I see him not:\nHe passeth on also, but I perceive him not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he seizeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the prey",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", who can hinder him?\nWho will say unto him, What doest thou?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God will not withdraw his anger;\nThe helpers of Rahab do stoop under him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How much less shall I answer him,\nAnd choose out my words ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to reason",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whom, though I were righteous, yet would I not answer;\nI would make supplication to my judge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I had called, and he had answered me,\nYet would I not believe that he hearkened unto my voice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he breaketh me with a tempest,\nAnd multiplieth my wounds without cause.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He will not suffer me to take my breath,\nBut filleth me with bitterness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "we speak",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of strength, lo, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mighty!\nAnd if of justice, Who, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saith he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", will summon me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though I be righteous, mine own mouth shall condemn me:\nThough I be perfect, it shall prove me perverse.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am perfect; I regard not myself;\nI despise my life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is all one; therefore I say,\nHe destroyeth the perfect and the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the scourge slay suddenly,\nHe will mock at the trial of the innocent.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The earth is given into the hand of the wicked;\nHe covereth the faces of the judges thereof:\nIf ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", who then is it?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now my days are swifter than a post:\nThey flee away, they see no good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They are passed away as the swift ships;\nAs the eagle that swoopeth on the prey.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I say, I will forget my complaint,\nI will put off my ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "sad",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " countenance, and be of good cheer;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am afraid of all my sorrows,\nI know that thou wilt not hold me innocent.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I shall be condemned;\nWhy then do I labor in vain?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I wash myself with snow water,\nAnd make my hands never so clean;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet wilt thou plunge me in the ditch,\nAnd mine own clothes shall abhor me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he is not a man, as I am, that I should answer him,\nThat we should come together in judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is no umpire betwixt us,\nThat might lay his hand upon us both.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let him take his rod away from me,\nAnd let not his terror make me afraid:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.9.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.9.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then would I speak, and not fear him;\nFor I am not so in myself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
